#include <iostream>
#include <fstream>
#include <string>

using namespace std;

int main() {
    string word; // word to search for
    int count = 0; // count of occurrences

    cout << "Enter the word to search for: ";
    cin >> word;

    ifstream file("filename.txt"); // replace filename.txt with actual file name

    if (file.is_open()) {
        string line;
        while (getline(file, line)) {
            size_t pos = line.find(word);
            while (pos != string::npos) {
                count++;
                pos = line.find(word, pos + 1);
            }
        }
        file.close();
    }
    else {
        cout << "Error opening file." << endl;
    }

    cout << "Number of occurrences of '" << word << "': " << count << endl;

    return 0;
}
```

2. Explanation:

-The program prompts the user to enter the word to search for.
-The program opens the specified text file using the ifstream object.
-The program reads the file line by line using the getline() function.
-For each line, the program searches for the specified word using the find() function.
-If the word is found, the program increments the count variable.
-The program continues searching for the word in the same line until it reaches the end of the line.
-The program then moves on to the next line and repeats the process.
-After all lines have been processed, the program closes the file and displays the total count of occurrences of the specified word.

3. Note:

-The program assumes that the specified word appears only once in each line of the file. If the word appears multiple times in a line, the count will only include the first occurrence.

-The program also assumes that the specified word appears only once in the entire file. If the word appears multiple times in the file, the count will only include the total number of occurrences.
